Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 01:23:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 134/174] feat: ccam pins screen-space sun shafts off;
 e_VolumetricFog defaults to 1 (ReCS)

eaa9d057 changed r_sunshafts' code default to 0 but the engine's sys_spec CVar group
Engine/Config/CVarGroups/sys_spec_PostProcessing.cfg:21 (r_SunShafts=2, [default] block,
inside engine.pak) re-applies 2 at startup, so the change was never seen.

CinematicCamera:
- New ApplySunShaftsOff() / RestoreSunShafts(): while the component drives the render state
  (CanDriveRenderState) it publishes SunShafts_Active = 0 on the post-effect bus - the parameter
  CTimeOfDay::UpdateEnvLighting writes and CSunShafts::Preprocess ANDs with the cvar - so the
  stage is off under the camera whatever the cfg set. Does not write r_sunshafts
  (VF_DUMPTODISK, global; decisions/s0-master-switch.md).
- Re-asserted every frame from CCinematicCameraPlugin::UpdateBeforeFinalizeCamera (after the
  TOD update), editor and game alike; latched once per activation with the existing
  save/restore pattern, restored in RestoreAllEffects, cleared by ClearSavedBaselines.
- Logs once per activation: "[CinematicCamera] sun shafts off (retired in favour of
  volumetric fog)".

Cry3DEngine:
- e_VolumetricFog default 0 -> 1 (VF_REQUIRE_APP_RESTART; help names the ReCS and stock
  defaults). No engine or project cfg sets it.

Docs: ConsoleReference.md (cfg override note under r_sunshafts, new e_VolumetricFog entry),
SceneReferredContent.md (section 1 table, section 3, section 5 quick table), README.

