+### e_VolumetricFog
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| ReCS default | **1** (on) |
+| Stock 5.7.1 default | 0 |
+| DLL | Cry3DEngine |
+| Purpose | Selects the volumetric (froxel) fog system for the whole level instead of the analytical global fog. `VF_REQUIRE_APP_RESTART`: a change takes effect only after the editor / launcher is restarted, it cannot be toggled live. On by default since 2026-09-09 because it is the god-ray source once the screen-space shafts are gone. No engine spec cfg sets it (`Engine/Config` and `Engine/Config/CVarGroups` grepped 2026-09-09), so the code default is what a fresh install runs; if a project's `system.cfg` / `game.cfg` or a cfg under `Engine/Config/CVarGroups/` ever sets it, that file wins and is the one to edit. |
+
+**How to get god rays on ReCS now.** `e_VolumetricFog` is on at its ReCS default, so after one
+restart the fog is running. Density comes from the Time of Day's volumetric fog `Global density`
+- the table in `SceneReferredCalibration.md` section 3.1 turns it into a visibility, and 0.1
+(haze, 3.9 km) to 0.4 (mist, 1 km) is where shafts read clearly. The two renderer cvars above are
+already at their ReCS defaults. A project that wants the analytical fog back sets
+`e_VolumetricFog 0` in its `system.cfg` and restarts.
 
